      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### How to read this dashboard\n\n**These are devices, not users.** One person on a Mac and a Windows laptop counts twice. The only identity a frontend metric carries is a per-browser `localStorage` UUID, surfaced as the `instance` label. Getting a real user count needs the preference stored server-side; it is not stored there today.\n\n**Only devices currently running the app are counted.** The state gauge is re-observed on every export tick (~60s), so someone who has glass on but has not launched today is invisible. Every absolute number here moves with desktop DAU — prefer the ratio panels.\n\n**\"No data\" is correct when no desktop renderer is running.** `count()` over an empty set returns nothing, not zero. It is also what a freshly deployed counter shows, because `increase()` needs two samples in the window.\n\n**Expect up to ~90s of blank panels after launching the desktop app.** The renderer exports every ~60s and VictoriaMetrics holds instant queries back by a 30s latency offset, so the first point is not visible immediately. If you need to confirm data is arriving before then, use `/api/v1/series` or a range query rather than an instant one.\n\n**On the `liquid` tier, disabling glass is currently a native no-op.** `setGlassEnabled` returns early for that tier (`apps/electron/src/window/glass.ts:336-341`) and `liquid-glass.ts` has no detach path, so the preference is saved and reported while the `NSGlassEffectView` stays attached. Read `turned_off` on `liquid` as that bug, not as dissatisfaction.\n\n**Nothing here says whether users like the effect.** A turn-off is equally consistent with \"looks bad\", \"hurt battery\" and \"was just curious\". That would need an explicit reason prompt.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.3.1",
      "title": "Read me first",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
